In modern hospitality management, maintaining consistent brand standards across daily shifts is one of the toughest operational challenges. General managers, department heads and floor leaders frequently deal with "ghost SOPs": tasks that are marked as completed on paper or in messaging groups without being physically executed on the floor.

[Mise](/) was built to solve this exact vulnerability.

Mise is the dedicated **hotel service execution platform (SEP)** designed to bring clarity, timing and accountability to daily hotel operations. Rather than creating new guidelines, the **Mise platform** implements the exact operational procedures your property already owns, transforming static documents into live, timed workflows on staff mobile devices.

## What makes Mise a service execution platform (SEP)?

A **service execution platform (SEP)** is an operational category built specifically for floor-level execution. Unlike traditional back-office tools or administrative software, a true SEP focuses entirely on active task verification, supervisor sign-offs and audit readiness.

### Core architecture of the Mise hotel platform

- **Timed task schedules:** Daily routines, from morning room inspections to evening security patrols, are delivered directly to staff phones as structured, time-sensitive assignments.
- **Mandatory photo proof:** To ensure accountability, staff attach real-time photo evidence directly inside the app before marking a task complete.
- **Remote supervisor sign-offs:** Floor managers and department heads can inspect work quality, review visual evidence and approve completed routines from anywhere in the property.
- **Zero PMS integration required:** The [Mise hotel platform](/platform) operates completely standalone, so hotels can deploy across departments without waiting for Property Management System (PMS) vendor setup or IT approvals.

## Why Mise is not an LMS or a PMS integration

To understand how the **Mise platform** fits into your hotel's technology, it helps to be clear about what Mise is *not*:

1. **Mise is not an LMS.** A Learning Management System (LMS) focuses on passive video courses and classroom training. Mise drives active, real-time task execution on the floor during live shifts.
2. **Mise requires zero PMS integration.** Property Management Systems manage guest reservations, billing and room folios. Mise focuses purely on shift execution, staff accountability and operational compliance, without touching your PMS.

## How Mise transforms hotel departments

Mise standardizes execution across every core hotel department:

- **Front office:** Streamlines duty manager shift handover logs, VIP arrival setups and guest request fulfillment.
- **Housekeeping:** Eliminates unverified cleaning checks by requiring photo proof for room turnarounds and public area maintenance.
- **Food & beverage and kitchen:** Runs temperature logs, buffet prep schedules and kitchen closing routines as timed tasks with evidence.
- **Engineering and safety:** Tracks preventive maintenance tasks, equipment inspections and perimeter security patrols with digital audit logs.

To see how the platform functions step by step, explore [how Mise works](/how-it-works) across live hotel shifts.

